From: thespine1337 <thespine1337@gmail.com>
Subject: Reset the logger when the MediaLibrary is destroyed

The logger set by the host is kept in a static (Log::s_logger). In VLC the
logger's class lives in libmedialibrary_plugin, which is unloaded on shutdown;
at process exit the static then calls a destructor that is no longer mapped
and the process crashes. Replace it with an IostreamLogger (Log::doLog() does
not check for a null logger).

--- a/src/MediaLibrary.cpp
+++ b/src/MediaLibrary.cpp
@@ -371,6 +371,9 @@
 MediaLibrary::~MediaLibrary()
 {
     stopBackgroundJobs();
+    // The logger provided by the host may live in a plugin that is unloaded
+    // before process exit; do not let the static outlive it.
+    Log::SetLogger( std::make_shared<IostreamLogger>() );
 }
 
 bool MediaLibrary::createAllTables()
